A||||5||Xtreme Fiero's||What up with my tach?||||1||
Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||09-21-2000||05:34 PM||||<BR>I have removed my Tach filter and taped off the wires. The tach usualy is at 0 rpm. but if I lay into it the tach will jump all over it never seems to drop below 0rpm or above 3k rpm. what could cause this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-21-2000||06:19 PM||||Guess that tach filter was there for a reason.  Get a Rodney Dickman replacement.||||reg||12
Z||000002||theogre||09-21-2000||07:49 PM||||could be picking up noise. could be a wire rubbed thru someplace and the vibration makeing a false signal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||09-23-2000||01:15 PM||||Could that be at reason the car surges at constat rpm? it'll surge hard enough to chirp the wheels in 2nd. but it will idle fine, it seels to miss a bit at WOT but the real problem in the surgeing during normal driveing. I'm hopeign to have it back on the road in "Good shape" by next weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||09-24-2000||12:14 AM||||The Haynes manual is telling me...<P>Engine surges while holding accelerator steady. (I'm assuming this means RPMs are not holding steady at a steady speed)<P>- intake air leak<BR>- fuel pump faulty<BR>- loose fuel injector harness connections<BR>- defective ECM<P>If your RPMs are steady and the tires are chirping then I'd say it could possibly be something in the tranny.  Prob the clutch... that's if your's is a stick.  I don't know, could be the lockup sensor too.  Maybe someone knows for sure what could cause that.<BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Conrad Sanville||09-24-2000||08:09 AM||||My 86 Gt was doing exactly the same thing a couple of weeks ago.  The tach went crazy while holding the throttle steady at cruising speed and would miss at that stage something awful. I started by changing the plug wires.  CURED THE PROBLEM...Hope that works for you. I really thought is was going to be something more serious, because the wires were really not that old.  Conrad<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
